WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.621
This is the order for setting up Gate Desk at your

00:00:03.621 --> 00:00:07.242
factory. It is a guided pilot checklist, not a recording of

00:00:07.242 --> 00:00:10.863
a completed factory installation. Use the Windows trial for these steps.

00:00:10.863 --> 00:00:14.485
The current Mac download checks compatibility; it is not a finished

00:00:14.485 --> 00:00:18.106
installer.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.182
Choose one computer as the factory host. It holds the accounts,

00:00:24.182 --> 00:00:28.865
original documents and counting model. Keep it powered on while phones

00:00:28.865 --> 00:00:33.548
need to send records. Do not create a different factory on

00:00:33.548 --> 00:00:38.231
every office computer. Keep the installed folder and its runtime data.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.488
Connect the recorder LAN port and computer to the same router

00:00:43.488 --> 00:00:47.476
or switch using Ethernet. Ask your CCTV installer for the supported

00:00:47.476 --> 00:00:51.464
local stream address and access details. Local video can work without

00:00:51.464 --> 00:00:55.452
internet when the equipment supports it and the local network stays

00:00:55.452 --> 00:00:59.441
powered. A cable alone is not enough.

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.579
Open CCTV Counter on the website and download the Windows trial.

00:01:05.579 --> 00:01:10.658
Extract the entire ZIP. Open the extracted folder and run Install

00:01:10.658 --> 00:01:15.737
Gate Desk dot cmd once. Then open the new desktop shortcut.

00:01:15.737 --> 00:01:20.816
Python, dependencies and the experimental bag model are included.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.059
On first launch, choose Set up this factory and create your

00:01:26.059 --> 00:01:30.118
owner account. If the factory already exists, sign in instead. Keep

00:01:30.118 --> 00:01:34.177
credentials private. The address one twenty seven dot zero dot zero

00:01:34.177 --> 00:01:38.237
dot one opens this computer. It is not the factory address

00:01:38.237 --> 00:01:42.296
to enter on a phone.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:48.151
After creating the owner account, stop the host cleanly. In the

00:01:48.151 --> 00:01:52.802
installed folder, run Configure Bundled Model dot cmd and authenticate as

00:01:52.802 --> 00:01:57.453
the owner. Follow its output before reopening the desktop launcher. The

00:01:57.453 --> 00:02:02.104
included model is experimental and bag only. It does not establish

00:02:02.104 --> 00:02:06.755
reliable beam, cloth or factory counts.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:12.713
In Account and Plans, open Camera setup. Enter the camera identifier,

00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:17.426
name, local address, stream port, path and credentials supplied for your

00:02:17.426 --> 00:02:22.139
recorder. Saving a draft does not start recording or prove counting.

00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:26.852
Before counting, verify the feed, source clock, recording retention, gaps and

00:02:26.852 --> 00:02:31.565
complete operation boundaries.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:37.983
Phone connection needs a real factory HTTPS address and a certificate

00:02:37.983 --> 00:02:42.966
trusted by the phone. This part still needs assisted setup and

00:02:42.966 --> 00:02:47.949
device testing. In Phone connection setup, enter the provisioned address, host

00:02:47.949 --> 00:02:52.932
IP, port and certificate file paths. Save settings only does not

00:02:52.932 --> 00:02:57.915
start the service. Complete the owner restart handoff, then verify reachability.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.312
Install the Android APK and open Gate Desk Dev. Enter the

00:03:04.312 --> 00:03:09.624
actual factory HTTPS address, tap Connect to factory, and sign in.

00:03:09.624 --> 00:03:14.936
A worker uses an owner-issued, expiring single-use invitation. APK files do

00:03:14.936 --> 00:03:20.248
not install on iPhone. Physical Android and iPhone acceptance is still

00:03:20.248 --> 00:03:25.560
pending. Installing the APK does not establish a working connection.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.142
Use a test gate pass first. Check its original document, quantity

00:03:32.142 --> 00:03:37.284
and units on the host. After enrollment, test saving offline and

00:03:37.284 --> 00:03:42.426
reconnecting. Wait for acknowledgment, and verify that a retry creates no

00:03:42.426 --> 00:03:47.568
duplicate. Compare a complete recorded operation with a manual count. Unknown

00:03:47.568 --> 00:03:52.710
counts must remain unknown, not zero or a final discrepancy.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.779
Finally, test outside factory Wi-Fi using mobile data. Off-site sync needs

00:03:58.779 --> 00:04:03.558
internet and a reachable receiving host. If the PC is off,

00:04:03.558 --> 00:04:08.337
phone records remain local and pending. Keep runtime data and backups;

00:04:08.337 --> 00:04:13.116
never delete records to troubleshoot. These checks are still required before

00:04:13.116 --> 00:04:17.895
treating Gate Desk as ready for factory use.
